   Also qualify the order statement: \(p\mid\Phi_e(r)\) implies \(e\mid p-1\) when \(p\nmid e\), with exceptional index-dividing primes handled separately.

7. **§4: GAP — FATAL to the stated sufficiency implication; other fixes MAJOR/MINOR.**

   **RT and the stated (O2) do not jointly suffice.** O2 recognizes factors in \(G\); RT only promises a smooth rational cofactor. It does not require that cofactor’s large prime factors to belong to \(G\). Restricting initial split primes to \(G\) does not control endogenous children.

   Fix this by requiring RT’s successful cofactors to factor over \(G\cup\{p\le B\}\), with uniform recognition guarantees and bounded-time rejection, or strengthen O2 to all relevant primes. Density alone cannot supply this compatibility.

