   566	- *Box.* With d = d(log q) as in §1.4, take the reduced-basis box of radius e^{σ_bE} of {(a, b) : a ≡ bm_d (mod q)}.
   567	- *Good point.* The box contains a primitive (a, b) such that:
   568	  - F_d(a, b) = a^d − sr^{j_d}b^d is e^{bE}-smooth;
   569	  - every prime factor of (a − bm_d)/q is ≤ e^{bE}, or lies in 𝒢 ∩ (e^{bE}, q^λ].
   570	
   571	The second condition is the **compatibility condition**: RT's large children must again be recognisable (codex
   572	snfsrig_2 #7, FATAL to the draft's sufficiency claim). It is vacuous when 𝒢 = all primes.
   573	
   574	RT is the rational-target-only, special-field case of [nest] Hypothesis AD. In the random-integer model it holds with
   575	room when 𝒢 has density 1 − o(1): the good-point margin is 5/6 for regular lattices and ≈ 1/2 in the worst case, and
   576	the union bound runs over e^{O(Q)} targets.
   577	
   578	**(O2) Recognition of 𝒢.** A rigorous procedure that finds every prime factor p ∈ 𝒢 of its input in expected time
   579	L_p[1/2, O(1)], for 𝒢 of density ≥ (log x)^{−O(1)} in every dyadic range up to L_N[2/3].
   580	- Unconditionally this is open (§5).
   581	- **Under RH, [g2rh] gives it with 𝒢 = all primes.** Then the compatibility condition is vacuous, and only (O1)
   582	  remains.
   583	
   584	**Also needed.**
   585	- Character columns at growing degree: ERH via [nest] Lemma X_ERH, or LV §6 unconditionally at cost L[1/3, Θ(δ)].
   586	- LV6 with one algebraic block per K_d ([nest] Prop R).
   587	- Multi-field square roots and the row algebra (Lemma RW, written in [nest] for a single field).
   588	
   589	These are UNVERIFIED bookkeeping. Note that [nest] Theorem NR cannot simply be specialised to a point-mass field law,
   590	because its recursive calls need the algorithm for all integers, which is (O2) again.
   591	
   592	**How far (O1) is from known results.**
   593	- **Algebraic half.**
   594	  - RT needs F_d(a, b) = a^d − sr^jb^d, of degree d growing up to O(D′), to be y-smooth with
   595	    log y ≍ (log|F|)^{1/2+o(1)}, so that u → ∞. And it needs this *pointwise* in special-q boxes.
   596	  - BBDT 2012 prove Ψ_F(x, y) ≍ x² for fixed degree-g forms only for y ≥ x^{g−2+ε} (x^{1/√e+ε} for cubics), with x the
   597	    variable size: power-size y and bounded u.
   598	  - Barbulescu–Lachand 2017, Thm 4.2, go down to y ≥ exp((log log x)^{5/3+ε}), but only for fixed primitive imaginary
   599	    *quadratic* forms of fundamental discriminant, in form-adapted regions, and without joint rational smoothness.
   600	  - None of these results establishes the required uniform statement.
   601	- **Rational half.**
   602	  - The values a − b·m_d with |a|, |b| ≤ V lie in the integers below m_dV whose residue mod m_d = r^{q_d} lies in
   603	    [0, V] ∪ [r^{q_d} − V, r^{q_d}). Up to endpoint corrections, a block of base-r digits in positions [log_r V, q_d)
   604	    is constant (all 0 or all r − 1).
   605	  - The prescribed proportion is (log m − log V)/(log m + log V) → 1. At the one-level design this is (1 − dν)/(1 + dν);
   606	    at α = 1/3 it is ≈ (D′ − φ_Fb)/(D′ + φ_Fb).
   607	  - RT tests (a − bm)/q, and division by q destroys the block. The relevant problem is therefore *multiples of q* with a
   608	    prescribed block whose cofactor is smooth.
   609	  - Bourgain (2013, 2015) and Swaenepoel (2020) prescribe only a small positive proportion of the digits of primes.
   610	  - None of these establishes even the rational half. Prop RB shows that statistics of smooth numbers alone cannot
   611	    replace it.
