   292	### 3.2 Algorithm H (unknown p; standard doubling)
   293	
   294	0. If N is even, output 2. Trial-divide by all primes ≤ 8100, and output any factor found.
   295	   (N is assumed composite and not a prime power. Perfect powers can be detected and split in
   296	   polynomial time by integer root extraction. A primality test can screen out prime N.)
   297	1. For j = 14, 15, … (so v_j = 2^j > 8100):
   298	   - set v_j := 2^j, w_j := ⌈L_{v_j}[1/2, 1]⌉, and h_j := ⌈L_{v_j}[1/2, 1 + ε(v_j)] (log N)³⌉,
   299	     where ε(v) := (log log v)^{−1/2};
   300	   - run Algorithm C h_j times with (v_j, w_j);
   301	   - output the first divisor found.
